      "mechanism_card": {
        "hypothesis": "GeoDAWN Area 2 was flown at 400 m E-W line spacing and 150-200 m terrain clearance (https://data.usgs.gov/datacatalog/data/USGS:657e1d85d34e23d3533209f7), so the H19-5 ridge positions that seeded R0 are uncertain by roughly the 300 m scoring-kernel radius. Where the smoothed TMI horizontal-gradient magnitude (band 3, tmi_hg) peaks within 2 px of an R0 dot, that crest is a better estimate of the magnetic-basement step (the fault) than the ridge seed, and re-centering dots on crests converts partial kernel credit into full credit.",
        "mechanism": "Move each of the 37,654 R0 dots <= 2 px (Euclidean, 13-pixel window) to the argmax of the 3x3-smoothed tmi_hg field; destination must stay inside the footprint at d_cat > 2 px (R0's own exclusion); count fixed; deterministic row-major processing, own-pixel-wins ties. DTI = T/(0.2T + 0.2(S-M) + 0.8|G|): mass S is unchanged, so only kernel credit T and the S-M term can move; a 100-200 m re-centering onto the true trace raises K_300 overlap on line-like truth (bar ~0.056 at DTI 0.28 for isolated truth, lower for lines).",
        "non_fault_mimic": "Flight-line corrugation residual between 400 m-spaced lines, cultural magnetics (pipelines, powerlines), Tertiary dike swarms and caldera ring-fracture crests, and sharp lithologic contacts all produce tmi_hg crests with no Quaternary fault; snapping can walk dots onto them.",
        "predicted_live_change": "+0.002 to +0.010 DTI [MODEL] vs R0 (treat |delta| < 0.01 on public chunks as no evidence).",
        "falsifier": "Live public score drops by >= 0.01 vs R0's receipt: the H19-5 ridge positions are already at or better than the tmi_hg crest, or snapping systematically walks dots onto non-fault crests."
      },
